{
  "id": "u14-l05",
  "unit": "u14-feelings-health",
  "title": "At the doctor",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "The doctor asks **আপনার কী সমস্যা?** 'What's the problem?' and answers with polite commands: **ওষুধ খান** 'take the medicine', **বিশ্রাম নিন** 'get some rest'. In Bengali you **eat** medicine (**ওষুধ খাওয়া**), just as you 'eat' water: **অনেক পানি খান** 'drink lots of water'.\n\nHow often: **দিনে তিন বার** 'three times a day'; here **বার** means 'times'. When: **খাওয়ার পরে** 'after meals', **খাওয়ার আগে** 'before meals'.\n\nAt home, a sister says it with তুই: **ওষুধ খা** (**খাও → খা**). Better again? **আমি এখন সুস্থ** 'I'm well now'.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "dine",
      "bn": "দিনে",
      "tr": "dine",
      "en": "a day; per day",
      "notes": "দিনে তিন বার 'three times a day'. Also 'in the daytime'."
    },
    {
      "id": "bar-times",
      "bn": "বার",
      "tr": "bar",
      "en": "times",
      "notes": "Counts how often: এক বার 'once', দুই বার 'twice', তিন বার 'three times'. Often written as one word (তিনবার). Same spelling as বার 'day of the week' (U5)."
    },
    {
      "id": "bishram",
      "bn": "বিশ্রাম",
      "tr": "bishram",
      "en": "rest",
      "notes": "বিশ্রাম নিন (আপনি) / নাও (তুমি) / নে (তুই) 'get some rest'."
    },
    {
      "id": "khawar",
      "bn": "খাওয়ার",
      "tr": "khawar",
      "en": "eating; meals",
      "notes": "খাওয়া 'eating' + -র: খাওয়ার পরে 'after meals', খাওয়ার আগে 'before meals'."
    },
    {
      "id": "shustho",
      "bn": "সুস্থ",
      "tr": "shustho",
      "en": "well; healthy",
      "notes": "Opposite of অসুস্থ 'ill'."
    },
    {
      "id": "kha",
      "bn": "খা",
      "tr": "kha",
      "en": "eat (intimate)",
      "notes": "তুই command: খাও → খা. Medicine is 'eaten' in Bengali: ওষুধ খা 'take your medicine'."
    }
  ],
